dwg2pdf 0.5.0 / GUI 0.2.20 -- COMPLETE release, 2026-09-18
================================================================

Everything needed to run, test and rebuild. Nothing omitted.

  dwg2pdf.py                 engine, revision 0.5.0
  dwg2pdf_gui.py             Qt GUI (qt.py -> PySide6), revision 0.2.20
  test_autocad.py            173 checks, runs anywhere
  test_gui.py                 79 checks, needs a Qt platform
  test_images.py              23 checks
  make_test_drawings.py      generates test_drawings/ and test_images/
  README.md                  the whole record, including section 9
  environment-dwg2pdf.yml    mamba/conda environment
  build_libredwg.sh          rebuilds the bundled decoder from source
  vendor/libredwg-win64/     LibreDWG 0.14.8593, Windows x86-64
  dwg_samples/               real DWGs, five source versions
  docs/                      screenshots referenced by the README

WHAT CHANGED IN 0.5.0 -- READ THIS BEFORE THE NEXT RUN
-----------------------------------------------------
1. accoreconsole now ANSWERS THE PROMPTS AutoCAD actually asks. The
   old fixed .scr assumed an order; AutoCAD asks 'Enter paper units'
   for some devices and not others, and one missing prompt shifted
   every later answer by one. The plot device was never the problem.
   --accore-mode script restores the old path for comparison.
2. acad-com NO LONGER ATTACHES to a running AutoCAD (--acad-attach
   opts back in). It used to plot through the session you were working
   in and then died with an access violation. It also recycles its own
   AutoCAD every 50 drawings (--acad-recycle-after).
3. The plot goes STRAIGHT TO THE DELIVERABLE. The 0.4.0 scratch rename
   defeated viewer locks but made the viewer report a missing file once
   per sheet -- a modal dialog is worse than a lock.
4. --layouts NOW DEFAULTS TO 'auto', not 'model'. Paper-space-only
   sheets were failing pass 1 for nothing and falling through to the
   slow AutoCAD passes.

INSTALL
-------
Unpack so that dwg2pdf.py and vendor/ are SIBLINGS. _find_tool()
resolves the bundled decoder relative to dwg2pdf.py, NOT to the
working directory. Verify:

    python dwg2pdf.py --probe

which must report:

    LibreDWG dwg2dxf 0.14.8593 at ...\vendor\libredwg-win64\dwg2dxf.exe [bundled]

Anything older than 0.13 means vendor/ is misplaced -- README 9.30.

TEST
----
    python test_autocad.py        # 173, no AutoCAD needed
    python test_gui.py            #  79
    python test_images.py         #  23

Fixtures are generated on first run, so these pass straight out of
the archive with no preparatory step.

GUI AND CLI ARE ONE CODE PATH (0.4.5 / 0.2.19)
----------------------------------------------
The GUI imports the engine and calls engine.run_batch(), the same
function the CLI calls. It has no serial loop, process pool or pass-2
retry of its own, so every engine fix reaches both by construction;
test_gui.py's check_engine_fix_coverage() asserts it.

